slowed more than expected in August as consumer prices posted their steepest monthly decline in four years, strengthening the case for the central bank to deliver another interest rate cut next week."]},{"type":"p","children":["Elsewhere, in the U.S. consumer prices accelerated in August as the cost of gasoline rebounded after two straight monthly declines, bolstering financial market expectations that the Federal Reserve could raise interest rates next week."]},{"type":"p","children":["Markets currently see an 85.4% chance of the Fed raising its interest rate at its meeting next week, up from 72.4% a day ago."]},{"type":"p","children":["\"Latin American central banks used to closely follow the Federal Reserve's policy moves, but since the pandemic they have become much more proactive and independent,\" said Malcolm Dorson, head of EM Strategy at Global X."]},{"type":"p","children":["\"Even if the Fed hikes next week, I expect Brazil to either remain on hold or cut. I think Mexico will remain on hold.\""]},{"type":"p","children":["Oil prices eased on Friday but remained north of $100 a barrel."]},{"type":"p","children":["While net oil exporters in the region have benefited from higher crude prices, fears persisted that prolonged inflation  could impact central bank policy outlooks."]},{"type":"p","children":["MEXICO STOCKS DIP"]},{"type":"p","children":["In the second largest economy of LatAm, Mexico, industrial output rose 0.5% in July from June and was 2.7% higher year-over-year, the national statistics agency said on Friday."]},{"type":"p","children":["The Mexican stocks benchmark index ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"BMV:ME","text":"BMV:ME"}}," dropped 0.4%. The peso ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"FX_IDC:USDMXN","text":"FX_IDC:USDMXN"}}," added 0.1%."]},{"type":"p","children":["MSCI's LatAm FX index (.MILA00000CUS) was trading 0.1% lower, as a stronger U.S. dollar following the inflation reading weighed on regional currencies."]},{"type":"p","chil